# Line-ending normalization (2026-08-26): repo was authored on Windows (CRLF) then migrated to
# Linux; declaring LF canonical + a one-time `git add --renormalize` ends the "thousands of files
# look modified" noise and the `git reset --hard` hazard. Content-preserving (verified: 0 non-CRLF changes).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never touch (leave git to detect, but pin the common ones so renormalize can't corrupt them).
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.h5 binary
*.npy binary
*.npz binary
*.pt binary
*.pyc binary

# Preserved from the prior .gitattributes: append-only provenance logs union-merge across branches.
research/findings/raw/_provenance/*.jsonl merge=union
